    "Optional root-only mReferenceUpdate receives final projected writeback and current settled flags, after own controllers, physics first synchronization/ordinary read and mProjected, before child controllers. The production owner must decide native publication eligibility and retain borrowed REFR and new placement; this callback alone does not implement World publication.",
    "Only this callback may change rendering placement during a pass. Capture and validate new unique invertible ancestor path, lease new ancestors, reanchor root drawing compensation to unchanged native cache, rebuild borrowed visitor path and invalidate old/new ancestor Skeletons before releasing old leases. Child native caches/drawing worlds remain unchanged until their own updates. Native author locals are unchanged by reanchor.",
